-- A file-dropping commit cancels nobody and invalidates nothing.  A
-- transaction open on the primary across the restore point gives the
-- anchor and every later snapshot on a segment the same xmin; an
-- unanchored REPEATABLE READ transaction whose executors hold that xmin
-- between statements survives the replayed TRUNCATE commit of another
-- table, where a resolution by xmin would have terminated them.  The
-- anchor stays.
----------------------------------------------------------------
