-- An executor that installed its anchor and opens its first relation only
-- after its segment replayed another table's TRUNCATE commit carries on:
-- the check is per relation.  The executor is held between the two by a
-- fault; the commit rewrites another table, so no lock waits anywhere and
-- the primary's commit is not held up.  The truncated table itself is
-- refused under the anchor until the next publication.
